questions.prompt:
Jokers always lie. Clowns always tell the truth.

A group of four, each of whom is a Joker or a Clown, make the following statements about each other:

- P says, "Q always lies";
- Q says, "R always lies";
- R says, "P always tells the truth";
- S says, "Exactly two of P, Q and R are Jokers".

How many of P, Q, R and S are Clowns?
